# Auth, URLs & Module Surfaces

## Roles (exactly three)

- `owner` — only `lingercoffee@gmail.com` under customer `81721200`; cross-tenant
- `admin` — single-customer super-admin; never other tenants or platform Maintenance
- `member` — own-user member surfaces only

Enforce at the controller layer — never UI-hiding alone.

## URL categories (exactly three)

- **admin** `/:cid/admin/` — `admin` or `owner`
- **member** `/:cid/member/` — `member` (GET/HEAD preview exception via `allow_admin_member_preview!`)
- **public** — everything else; no auth required

## Module surfaces (exactly four)

1. Entries → `/:customer_id/modules/<module_key>`
2. Customer settings → `/:customer_id/settings/modules/<module_key>`
3. Enable/disable → `/:customer_id/maintenance/modules`
4. Platform settings → `/:customer_id/maintenance/module_settings` (owner / `81721200` only)
